.SH NAME
site \- a logical object definition in the xCAT database.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBsite Attributes:\fR  \fIinstalldir\fR, \fImaster\fR, \fIxcatdport\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Logical objects of this type are stored in the xCAT database in one or more tables.  Use the following commands
to manipulate the objects: \fBmkdef\fR, \fBchdef\fR, \fBlsdef\fR, and \fBrmdef\fR.  These commands will take care of
knowing which tables the object attributes should be stored in.  The attribute list below shows, in
parentheses, what tables each attribute is stored in.
.SH "site Attributes:"
.IX Header "site Attributes:"
.IP "\fBinstalldir\fR (site.value)" 6
.IX Item "installdir (site.value)"
The installation directory
.IP "\fBmaster\fR (site.value)" 6
.IX Item "master (site.value)"
The management node
.IP "\fBxcatdport\fR (site.value)" 6
.IX Item "xcatdport (site.value)"
Port used by xcatd daemon on master
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBmkdef\|(1)\fR, \fBchdef\|(1)\fR, \fBlsdef\|(1)\fR, \fBrmdef\|(1)\fR
